 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Most likely, the layer of varnish and gloss is what's causing it. When the varnish dries, it absorbs the air, so it's a little flatter. A simple white piece of paper held up to the light shows the difference. A white piece with a sheen looks white, a white piece with a flat glare. You can add a layer of varnish, or a high gloss paint, to get that sheen back. Just be sure the surface is clean first, so the varnish sticks.",
